---
args: { turn: ApprenticeshipTurn }
returns: ApprenticeshipTurnResult
---
1. Bind replay = inspectTurnIdentifier(turn). If replay.status is replay and replay.receipt is not null, bind saved = replay.receipt and return { sessionId: turn.sessionId, status: 'simulated', utterance: saved.utterance, typedAction: saved.typedAction, transition: saved.transition, challenge: saved.challenge, debrief: saved.debrief, blockers: [], checkpoint: turn.checkpoint, replayed: true, commitAllowed: false }. Do not rerun classification, schedule a challenge, or call checkpointTurn; never rewind later checkpoint history.
2. If replay.status is conflict, unresolved, or replay with a null receipt, bind status to 'replay-conflict' for conflict and 'replay-unresolved' otherwise. Bind blockers to replay.blockers, adding the missing complete receipt as an explicit blocker for a null replay receipt. Return { sessionId: turn.sessionId, status, utterance: null, typedAction: null, transition: null, challenge: null, debrief: null, blockers, checkpoint: turn.checkpoint, replayed: false, commitAllowed: false }. A legacy applied ID without a complete receipt is unresolved; changed input under a stored ID is conflict.
3. Bind utterance = interpretTraineeUtterance(turn). Return its child classification and any visible-fact answer in every new-turn path.
4. If utterance.kind.kind is question, return { sessionId: turn.sessionId, status: 'question-answered', utterance, typedAction: null, transition: null, challenge: null, debrief: null, blockers: [], checkpoint: turn.checkpoint, replayed: false, commitAllowed: false }. Do not match an operation, advance the world, schedule a challenge, or change the checkpoint.
5. If utterance.kind.kind is ambiguous, return { sessionId: turn.sessionId, status: 'clarification-needed', utterance, typedAction: null, transition: null, challenge: null, debrief: null, blockers: utterance.clarificationNeeded, checkpoint: turn.checkpoint, replayed: false, commitAllowed: false }.
6. For an action proposal only, bind typedAction = matchPermittedProcedureStep(utterance, turn). If typedAction.status is clarification, return { sessionId: turn.sessionId, status: 'clarification-needed', utterance, typedAction, transition: null, challenge: null, debrief: null, blockers: typedAction.clarificationNeeded, checkpoint: turn.checkpoint, replayed: false, commitAllowed: false }. Never send a clarification action to world advancement.
7. Bind transition = advanceTrainingWorldOnce(typedAction, turn). Unsafe proposals receive only an in-simulator refusal or approved training consequence; nothing dispatches to real equipment.
8. Bind challenge = scheduleFairScenarioChange(transition, turn, turn.sourceScenario). Derive the learning target from the preserved source scenario and saved seed while varying only surface context; retain earlier facts so a correct previous decision cannot become retroactively wrong.
9. Bind debrief = compareObservedProcedure(turn.actionHistory, typedAction, transition, challenge). Keep the typed action as the plan, the returned transition as simulated execution evidence, and history as separately observed learner actions. Never treat an unobserved plan as a performed step.
10. Bind binding = { sessionId: turn.sessionId, turnId: turn.turnId, sourceScenario: turn.sourceScenario, utterance: turn.utterance, sourceEvidence: turn.sourceEvidence, authorityStatus: turn.authorityStatus, actor: turn.actor, world: turn.world, procedure: turn.procedure, scenarioFamily: turn.scenarioFamily, learningObjective: turn.learningObjective, seed: turn.seed, actionHistory: turn.actionHistory }.
11. Bind receipt = { binding, utterance, typedAction, transition, challenge, debrief }. Bind checkpoint = checkpointTurn(turn.checkpoint, receipt). Return { sessionId: turn.sessionId, status: 'simulated', utterance, typedAction, transition, challenge, debrief, blockers: [], checkpoint, replayed: false, commitAllowed: false }.
